{"name":"Saluki Bronze","hex":"#65492a","fetched":"2026-10-24","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bronze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A naturally occurring or man-made alloy of copper, usually in combination with tin, but also with one or more other metals.","A reddish-brown colour, the colour of bronze."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of bronze metal.","Having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saluki","blocks":[{"text":"The Saluki or Arabian hound or Persian hound is a standardised breed developed from sighthounds – dogs that hunt primarily by sight rather than strong scent – that was once used by nomadic tribes to run down game animals. The dog was originally bred in the Fertile Crescent. The modern breed is typically deep-chested and long-legged, and similar dogs appear in medieval and ancient art. The breed is most closely related to the Afghan Hound, a basal breed that predates the emergence of modern breeds in the 19th century, and the Saluki has been purebred both in the Middle East, including by royalty, since at least that era, and in the West since the 1840s, though as a free-breeding landrace, similar dogs are common as feral animals in the Middle East. A related standardised breed is the north African Sloughi.\nThe saluki is one possible explanation for the mythical Set animal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg/330px-Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saluki","wikidata":"Q39108"},{"title":"Bronze","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is an alloy consisting primarily of copper, commonly with about 12–12.5% tin and often with the addition of other metals and sometimes non-metals or metalloids. These additions produce a range of alloys some of which are harder than copper alone or have other useful properties, such as strength, ductility, or machinability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg/330px-Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze","wikidata":"Q34095"},{"title":"Bronze (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is a metallic brown color which resembles the metal alloy bronze. An archaic term for it was aeneous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png/330px-Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_(color)","wikidata":"Q2778382"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg/500px-Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg/1280px-Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg/500px-Red_Smooth_Saluki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Smooth_Saluki.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Cream_saluki_on_grass.jpg/500px-Cream_saluki_on_grass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Cream_saluki_on_grass.jpg/1280px-Cream_saluki_on_grass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Cream_saluki_on_grass.jpg/500px-Cream_saluki_on_grass.jpg?utm_source=en.wi